==English==

{{slim-wikipedia|dab=Stair}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|staire|lang=enm}}, {{term|stayre|lang=enm}}, {{term|stayer|lang=enm}}, {{term|steir|lang=enm}}, {{term|steyre|lang=enm}}, {{term|steyer|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|stǣġer||stair, staircase}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*staigriz||stairs, scaffolding}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*steygʰ-||to walk, proceed, march, climb}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|steiger||a stair, step, wharf, pier, scaffolding|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|steiger|lang=gml}}, {{term|steir||scaffolding|lang=gml}}. Related to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term/t|ang|āstǣgan||to ascend, go up, embark}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term/t|ang|stīgan||to go, move, reach; ascend, mount, go up, spring up, rise; scale}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Stiege||a flight of stairs|lang=de}}. More at {{l|en|sty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-stair.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɛə(r)}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|stare}}
[[File:Entrance stairway of persepolis.JPG|thumb]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A single [[step]] in a [[staircase]].
# A [[series]] of steps, a staircase.

====Usage notes====
* ''Stairs'' and ''stair'' are used to refer to a single staircase, mostly interchangeably in the UK.

